From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Reserve queue slots for what cannot be lost

The scheduler's interrupt queue holds eight messages and serves three things at
once: our retrace edges, our SP and DP edges, and -- through the command queue
that __scHandleRetrace drains -- the game's own task submissions. One retrace too
many takes the place of a task completion.

A first attempt refused to deposit a retrace while the previous one was still
undelivered. It stopped the game from booting at all: our external queue is not
drained on a schedule but **opportunistically**, when a guest thread happens to
wait, so the flag stayed set and every later retrace was discarded. Any policy
that assumes periodic draining is wrong here by construction.

This looks at the guest queue's actual state at deposit time and keeps nothing
between passes. On hardware a retrace raised while the queue is full is lost the
same way -- osSendMesg is called without blocking from the interrupt.

Measured on Windows 95, before and after:

    before   1 task submitted, 1 SP edge, 0 display lists
    after   170 tasks, 169 SP edges, 61 DP edges, 547 display lists,
            17 audio voices normalised, 3540 frames presented

The game now runs its audio engine and submits display lists. The remaining
crash is further along, in __scHandleRDP.

diff --git a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
--- a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
@@ -210,6 +210,32 @@
     }
 
     while (external_messages.try_dequeue(to_send)) {
+        // **Reserver deux places pour ce qui ne peut pas etre perdu.**
+        //
+        // La file d'interruptions du planificateur tient huit messages et sert a
+        // la fois nos retraces, nos bords SP et DP, et — par la file de
+        // commandes que `__scHandleRetrace` draine — le demarrage des taches du
+        // jeu. Un retrace de trop y prend la place d'une fin de tache.
+        //
+        // Une premiere tentative refusait le depot d'un retrace tant que le
+        // precedent n'etait pas delivre. Elle a bloque le demarrage : notre file
+        // externe n'est pas drainee a intervalle regulier mais **opportunement**,
+        // quand un fil invite se met en attente, et le drapeau restait pose. Une
+        // politique qui suppose un drainage periodique est fausse par
+        // construction ici.
+        //
+        // On regarde donc l'etat reel de la file invitee au moment du depot,
+        // sans rien retenir entre deux passages. Sur le materiel, un retrace
+        // emis alors que la file est pleine est perdu de la meme facon —
+        // `osSendMesg` y est appele sans blocage depuis l'interruption.
+        if (to_send.source == ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Vi &&
+            to_send.mq != NULLPTR) {
+            const OSMesgQueue* q = TO_PTR(OSMesgQueue, to_send.mq);
+            if (q->msgCount > 2 && q->validCount >= q->msgCount - 2) {
+                complete_delivery(to_send.delivery);
+                continue;
+            }
+        }
         const bool sent = do_send(PASS_RDRAM to_send.mq, to_send.mesg, to_send.jam, false);
         // **Compter les depots, pas les demandes.**
         //
